  "source_commit": "7cbf7a0c32fca1badf05931879a37c3f8a2b03b4",
  "scope": "Independent mathematical and literal-source-contract review of OCH15-OCH30. OCH1-OCH14 are preceding inputs and are independently reviewed by root; their proof is not recertified here. This review supports the exact selected OneChar implication, retaining the separate AUT_UNRAM_COEF antecedent and all inherited foundational boundaries.",
  "findings": [
    "OCH15: Strict localness implies boundedness and adic continuity on the actual complete Noetherian ring. Finite coordinate images give one finite coefficient field. The prime-to-ell finite inertia average is invertible by strict residual congruence. The full-inertia polynomial and ordered-product identities, followed by the distinct-eigenvalue flag and conjugate-place argument, preserve the original IsPt and local potential-crystalline scope.",
    "OCH15/OCH20: The requested automatic-continuity clarification for an arbitrary dual-number algebra map is present. Finite scalar extension to a valuation ring containing the small first coordinates, followed by the exact formal Taylor identity modulo (X_i-a_i)^2, determines the map by finitely many second coordinates. It proves continuity in a finite coefficient algebra without adding a continuity hypothesis to the original all-maps quantifier.",
    "OCH16: The normalized difference has three distinct eigenvalues; its strict residual congruence excludes opposite marked scalars. Coordinate-subspace enumeration gives precisely type I or the irreducible outer block. The diagonal intertwiner equations give the actual T(t) conjugacy, including the square-root case when all odd-weight entries vanish, and extend it from G_K to the full disconnected group.",
    "OCH17: Prime-to-ell reduction and the original inertia unit identify the ordered finite characters. The gs argument treats inertia elements without the unit property. The remaining strict-near-one character factors through the ideal class group and is trivial under the original ell-coprime class-number condition; the normalized point is exactly the base.",
    "OCH18: The restriction of an irreducible finite-dimensional representation to the normal cyclotomic kernel is semisimple by the sum of conjugates of a simple submodule. Its nontrivial commuting algebra gives a common eigenmatrix and a nontrivial self-twist of the full abelian quotient. The infinite cyclotomic inertia argument contradicts trace zero; no finite-layer irreducibility is substituted.",
    "OCH19: The negative matrix-weight characters are precisely Psi^j and eta*Psi^j; their local finite condition and the inherited global strict rank-one theorem give vanishing. Weight zero reduces to unramified additive characters over K, which vanish by finite class group, and finite-quotient averaging. Individual finite coefficient fields and primitives descend through KTR1.",
    "OCH20: The tangent is the actual normalized cocycle, with full local finite kernels. Period primitives and graph comparison apply after the finite-coefficient continuity argument. The normalization equations force its primitive to lie in Qbar_ell*diag(1,0,-1); no unprovided fixed-field bound is asserted.",
    "OCH21: Compared directly with the reduced InpZ ptHyp_of contract. The type-I twist rho_K*epsilon^-1 has exactly the alternating-component adjoint convention -J X^t J and pairing multiplier epsilon^(1-3). OCH18 supplies the full infinite-cyclotomic irreducibility for ADK6. Type II uses the actual W and universal IsExt scope of the same LemW to apply KTR13. All three PtHyp fields concern the same ring and marked datum.",
    "OCH22: The two branches satisfy every original Adm3/Adm2 field. The rank-two ramified-quadratic case uses gcd(N,disc K)=1 and the order-two inertia quotient, giving exactly N*abs(disc K). The ell-place ordered outer line, determinant, weights e and -e and noncyclotomic ratios give the literal Level alternative. The direct-sum isomorphism is the actual coordinate permutation.",
    "OCH23: Canonical normalization at g1 is well-defined on cohomology, additive and injective. A b-torsion class has b-torsion normalized values. The local inertia unit forces a local primitive to be b-torsion too, so a=b is allowed. The line E10-E21 has the full disconnected character Psi^-1, and the c/g1/cg1^-1c normalization and Kill/local primitive conditions give precisely shaCoc.",
    "OCH24: The square-zero representation (1+epsilon*gamma)r0 has the exact multiplication, normalization and local comparison map. The integral local weight-minus-one primitive and OCH8 give the original It condition; OCH14 supplies the integral derivation lift. Actual entry derivatives are Psi(g)^(w_j)*gamma(g)_ij. Injectivity and additivity require only the original additive scope.",
    "OCH25: The SP1 lower bound applies to every torsion layer before any finite-length conclusion. Compact-to-discrete cocycles have finite image and hence are torsion; the increasing union length is the supremum because each finite strict chain is witnessed in one torsion layer. RV1 identifies the exact shaFam(ell*N) quotient and Vlen, allowing infinity throughout this step.",
    "OCH26: All M1-M5 concern the same A,Q,q and trace element. Nonpositive-weight rigidity kills the actual tangent through its normalized primitive; entry density proves the cotangent assertions. The point and two-derivation conditions retain their original torus rescaling and dimension-one scope. M2 is the finite quotient weight-zero module, not finiteness of the ambient A0.",
    "OCH27: SP6 is reapplied to the final irredundant covering set, rather than discarding summands from a previous estimate. Restriction along q preserves coverage and is injective on actual orbit representatives, so no multiplicity is introduced. The generic valuation is e_O*v_ell and division by e_O gives exactly the original factor-two normalized inequality.",
    "OCH28: One invocation of the original automorphy antecedent supplies the same marked g1 with FinA, AutB and LemW. The finite upper bound proves Selmer finiteness before taking toNat. The actual representation set X is injectively indexed by the chosen point representatives using OCH16; its pairwise-isomorphism condition and base trace t=Psi(sigma)+1+Psi(sigma)^-1 match OneChar exactly.",
    "OCH29: The prime-to-ell character values lie in one unramified coefficient valuation ring inside the fixed algebraic closure. The proof preserves all actual values, primary components, kernels and GD guards. It does not assert an embedding of the whole original possibly ramified coefficient ring into the new one.",
    "OCH30: Direct comparison with KatoQuadraticCharacters/OneChar.lean confirms the exact implication InpZ -> AutomorphyUnramifiedCoefficients -> OneChar. RV7 transfers finiteness and normalized Vn while the same actual finite set X, fixed iota, sigma and t are retained. AUT_UNRAM_COEF remains a separate producer. The proposed selected implication closure is not an unconditional OneChar or RH/GRH closure."
  ],
  "resolved_findings": [
    {
      "claims": [
